Backport the Qt signal/slot publication fixes from:

  d96da673e1e15a44b8dce8a0accc9f9bc194f4b5
  QObject::connect: fix tsan issue with signalVector

  2bdad17a2cf1475819057e2eb564e4904152daa5
  QObject::connect: strengthen some of the atomic machinery

  b2daed079984952d1617b6b696d110efc288b3b3
  QObject: fix TSAN data race between resizeSignalVector and doActivate

  be31faf39a824f79a1ad8e676512365b59448bea
  QObject::doActivate: fix tsan-reported issue with maybeSignalConnected

  b295841f70fd4313fc19464681ace39c1d9303ba
  QObjectPrivate::Connection(List): storeRelaxed the contained atomics

These changes fix QTBUG-146900 and QTBUG-146986. Qt 5.15 has the same
lock-free signal activation design but publishes connection data, resized
signal vectors, and newly inserted connections with relaxed atomics. It also
retains ConnectionData only after the early connectivity check and byte-copies
ConnectionList atomics while resizing. Concurrent connection, activation, and
sender teardown can therefore expose uninitialized or freed connection state.
Queued-argument metadata has the same publication gap: one emitter initializes
and atomically publishes the type array while another acquire-less emitter
immediately dereferences it.

Adapt qobject_p_p.h changes to Qt 5.15's qobject_p.h layout, retain the Qt 5
Connection ref-count initialization, and complete the release/acquire and
lifetime pairs at the corresponding publication boundaries. Acquire-load the
queued-argument pointer so it pairs with testAndSetOrdered() publication.

